There are 6 examples, and each batch holds 2. These numbers divide evenly.

```javascript
const examples = 6;
const batchSize = 2;
const batchesPerEpoch = examples / batchSize;
console.log(batchesPerEpoch);
```

It prints 3. Three batches cover the six examples once. The code counts batches; it does not train a model.
